Asymmetric. Yeah, asymmetric couch co-op.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:39.000
I mean, it's sort of like Sonic in Tails, but worse?

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.320
Not worse. Less emphasis on the Tails, you know?

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.300
He was almost like another Sonic, whereas in this it's your bird.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.720
I think he's a falcon.

00:01:51.820 --> 00:02:03.120
It seems asymmetric in the sense, I mean, in a lot of senses, but one of the senses is definitely that like one character is a lot more robust in his like options than the other.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:14.000
Yeah, it's like if you had to give, like if you didn't just give your little brother an unplugged controller, but you wanted to minimize the damage he could do, you'd play 8-Eyes.

00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:24.620
But I will say that I think that there's definitely a lot of potential for actual like help to become from second player.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.340
You know, like I don't think it's like, I'm trying to think of another example.

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:35.140
You know, like, I mean, it's not exactly the same because it's not co-op, but like Duck Hunt, we found out you can plug in the other controller and control the ducks.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.840
And it's like you barely even notice that there's a difference.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:43.900
Yeah. And this is like, okay, you can be a significant help as player too.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:49.960
Yeah. And I don't know about you guys, but whenever I play a game for Nostalgia, I try to go in as blind as possible.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.480
And when I first started playing 8-Eyes, I was like, oh, this is just another one of those side scrolling action games.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.840
Like it felt like a Castlevania clone in some ways.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.060
But instead of a whip, you have a sword.

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.800
