00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.860
Like it wasn't even obvious to me at first that I was the one doing it.

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:10.800
It felt like a mistake.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:13.600
Like, oh, the Falcon's moving when I'm moving and stuff like that.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:22.980
And then I realized like, oh, there's a whole like control scheme for a one player to be both the hero and the Falcon at the same time.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.500
It does work better with two players, no doubt.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:34.020
But they give you the option to, you know, I think that's better than having a computer controlled AI Falcon.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:39.880
Like if the game is built for two players to one be, you know, one be the hero, one be the Falcon.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.440
As a one player experience, you can still try to bring in the reins as both of them.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:52.320
Yeah, I read the manual before I booted it up and it was describing sort of how they were going to go about this.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:56.640
Um, and I was kind of intimidated by what they were saying.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:00.580
Like, it's almost like a trope, uh, on this podcast.

00:04:00.580 --> 00:04:04.400
