And the things hidden in the wall are easy to do when it's just you, you know, like as a single player thing where it's like,

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.180
all right, now I got to be the Falcon for a second.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:58.580
Like that, that part's achievable, but the, um, the attacking part is more like, uh, you know, you want to be on, uh,

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:03.580
you almost want to be like on the staircase below them and then take control of the Falcon and start, and start fighting.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:08.440
So that kind of stuff proved really useful, but I do think that the Falcon still feels like a, a little brother.

00:06:09.020 --> 00:06:15.620
See, I, I'm, I found that there were, there were enemies that weren't even, I mean, I noticed the enemies that you could only attack with the Falcon,

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:22.060
but there were some that you could choose both that I thought it was just more efficient to use the Falcon based on their positioning or like,

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:26.240
oh, I'm going to jump down. I'm going to get stabbed immediately just because it's like one of those traps sort of,

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:29.040
but I can send the Falcon down there and he sort of flies above.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:36.600
Um, so like I, I found it almost equal playing solo of times I wanted to use the, maybe not equal.

