00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:42.440
But as, but as we're going to get into, I'm not quite sure that, uh, two player asymmetrical co-op is enough, uh, to go through everything, uh, that this game offers.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.380
It's not, it's not enough of a cool factor.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:50.540
And, um, I think no better way to start than to just, uh, walk through like how the game kind of lays itself out.

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:58.000
And that is that it takes the, uh, I always call it the Mega Man style of approach where you can, uh, select the stage you want to go to.

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:06.180
There are eight castles, each with an evil duke who controls one of the eight jewels, not eyes, but the jewels are the eyes, the jewels are their eyes.

00:10:06.300 --> 00:10:07.760
I don't know. Uh, but that's the idea.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:09.280
You're collecting these jewels from these dukes.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:16.780
You got to go to eight different castles and the order that you go to them, unlike Mega Man kind of does matter.

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:23.260
See, when you defeat a duke, you get, uh, you get a sword of a certain like color.

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:29.940
And then that sword is only powerful on one specific duke in another castle.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:34.020
And if you don't go immediately to that duke, you'll lose that sword.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:37.000
Uh, for whatever reason, you can't like have an inventory of your swords.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:42.220
You just get the next color and you drop, like, let's say you picked up the green, you just drop the green and grab the red.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:43.640
And now you have to figure out that.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:50.280
So there is an actual like optimal, uh, order level, which you could argue Mega Man does.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:54.240
But what I'm saying is that Mega Man gives you the freedom to say, I want this power up.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.520
And then you have it for the remainder of the game.

00:10:57.240 --> 00:11:01.940
Uh, eight eyes takes a different approach where it says, no, you're just going to get this duke's sword.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:08.440
And then if you don't use it on the other correct duke, get ready for a grind fest boss battle.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:15.140
Yeah. Like it's, it's mostly, um, like it's just a way to pad the length.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.840
